# Interaction feedback and motion

Read [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md) → Motion, Interaction guidelines, Board-first interaction law.

## Principle

Feedback must tell the **truth** about state. If it looks clickable, it is. If it looks loading, something is in flight. If it looks disabled, say why.

## Required feedback channels

| Phase | Must communicate |
|---|---|
| **Hover / focus** | Affordance on interactive chrome only — not hover-only essentials |
| **Press / active** | Acknowledgement without fake depth (no universal lift) |
| **Loading** | Real wait; no fake progress bars |
| **Success / error** | Inline or status; not blocking celebration |
| **Reduced motion** | `prefers-reduced-motion` and `data-motion="reduced"` win |

Touch-first: generous targets; keyboard focus via `:focus-visible`.

## Motion

Motion explains **continuity** — a piece moved, a card flipped, a die landed.

| Layer | Rule |
|---|---|
| **Chrome** | ~140ms ease-out on backgrounds; no entrance motion on shell surfaces |
| **Game objects** | Shared tabletop primitives (lift, drop, deal, flip, fan, stack, roll, snap) |
| **Playful** | Longer/bouncier via `data-motion="playful"` — opt-in, not default noise |

Default duration band: **~200ms** for object motion; chrome stays shorter.

## Forbidden motion tells

- Fake progress or shimmer on instant actions
- AI-default fade/lift/shimmer on every tile and button
- Hover-lift on catalogue chrome
- Motion that **gates** input — animate after honouring the move
- Unskippable celebration sequences

**Animation half-life:** first hour teaches; hundredth hour waits. Prefer skippable/summarisable effects.

## Board-first

Moves happen on the board. Pew buttons are shortcuts and confirmations, not a parallel move grid.

Conflicts: favour **intentionality** and physical tabletop read over decorative motion.
